.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
.local/
.runtime/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
.venv/
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.sqlite*
*.db
*.jsonl
# The mover v3 run log, holdout access log and amendment files are append-only records that every run requires to be
# committed and pushed (blueprints/us-equities/mover-v3/protocol-core-draft.json, run_discipline).
!blueprints/us-equities/mover-v3/*.jsonl
!blueprints/us-equities/mover-v3/data/*.jsonl
# Sanitized Codex --json event streams retained as receipt evidence (client configuration output withheld).
!evidence/artifacts/codex-use-20260926-5/*.jsonl
!evidence/artifacts/codex-use-20260926-6/*.jsonl
# The model-server gates' per-run Codex event streams: the frozen pass rule is scored on them and both receipts
# inventory them by hash.
!evidence/artifacts/local-model-server-gate-20261001/runs/*/events.jsonl
!evidence/artifacts/local-model-server-gate-confirmatory-20261001/runs/*/events.jsonl
# The local-model measurement's per-case validity files and per-query nDCG@10 files: both decision statistics reproduce
# from them, and both receipts inventory them by hash (evidence/artifacts/new-wsl-local-models-20261002/README.md).
!evidence/artifacts/new-wsl-local-models-20261002/part-a/logs/*/validity.jsonl
!evidence/artifacts/new-wsl-local-models-20261002/part-b/runs/*/per-query.jsonl
# Codex app-server hooks/list oracle answers behind scripts/adoption_status.py's Codex model (throwaway homes shown
# as $BASE, no hash value): evidence/artifacts/adoption-status-truth-20260926/README.md.
!evidence/artifacts/adoption-status-truth-20260926/*.jsonl
# native_token_ci.py's committed synthetic Claude usage-log fixture for the ccusage
# CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR fixture (docs/token-efficiency-stack.md#hosted-ci-coverage-2026-09-26):
# clearly labelled synthetic content, not host history.
!fixtures/ccusage-synthetic-claude/**/*.jsonl
# The OmniRoute gateway's sanitized SEARCH log lines (queries and provider only, no ids), retained as receipt evidence:
# evidence/artifacts/omniroute-gateway-20260927/README.md.
!evidence/artifacts/omniroute-gateway-20260927/*.jsonl
# PR-H's frozen public synthetic log fixture (blind-lane positive control and
# seed-log-symbol tasks, evidence/artifacts/token-adoption-e2e-20260926/preregistration.json):
# clearly labelled synthetic content, not host history.
!evidence/artifacts/token-adoption-e2e-20260926/fixtures/*.jsonl
# The GraphQL pull-request pages (P) that docs/decisions/2026-10-03-macos-ci-scope.md's replay reads, inventoried by
# hash in evidence/artifacts/macos-ci-scope-20261003/README.md.
!evidence/artifacts/macos-ci-scope-20261003/prs_graphql.jsonl
adoption/hosts/*.json
!adoption/hosts/example.json
!adoption/hosts/macos-example.json

# scripts/host_receipts.py review: a stable per-receipt flock anchor (never deleted, to
# avoid the classic lockfile-deletion race) and the temp file its atomic os.replace() write
# uses; process coordination artifacts, never evidence.
evidence/hosts/**/*.json.lock
evidence/hosts/**/*.json.tmp-*

# Generated public explorer (scripts/build_ecosystem.py --write); rebuilt
# locally or downloaded from the publish-catalog.yml release artifact/
# attestation, never committed. See docs/decisions/2026-09-23-generated-
# explorer-sorted-manifest.md.
/docs/ecosystem/index.html

# Claude Code: personal project-local settings, and the worktrees
# `claude --worktree` creates inside the repository.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
# Serena's generated per-project index/config/logs can contain private host paths.
.serena/

# ai-memory's capture opt-in is each host's own decision, never committed; .worktreeinclude
# copies it into new worktrees (recipes/README.md, "Worktrees and the capture marker").
/.ai-memory.toml

# Credential-shaped files never belong in a checkout; secrets live under
# ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/native-agent-stack (docs/secret-storage.md).
*.env
*.key
*.pem
.credentials.json
auth.json
hosts.yml
.netrc
stored_tokens

# Hugging Face's other file, the active token, has the bare basename `token`.
# That name is deliberately not listed here: it is too generic to ignore
# repository-wide (it would silently hide an unrelated tracked file with that
# exact name). scripts/credential_status.py's SENSITIVE_BASENAME makes the
# same choice (docs/secret-storage.md "Threat model").
